+# Gate external content before LlamaIndex memory persistence
+
+The Result Claim Audit wrapper targets the current `VectorMemory.put` and
+`VectorMemory.set` boundary. It runs before `_commit_node()` reaches
+`vector_index.insert_nodes()`.
+
+```python
+from llama_index.core.memory.vector_memory import VectorMemory
+from llamaindex_result_claim_audit import ResultClaimAuditedMemory
+
+memory = ResultClaimAuditedMemory(VectorMemory.from_defaults())
+memory.put(
+    message,
+    provenance={
+        "trust": "quarantined",
+        "origin": "rag",
+        "actor_kind": "retriever",
+        "source_record_id": "node-7",
+        "source_ref": "https://example.test/node-7",
+    },
+)
+```
+
+Accepted receipts are stored in the native `ChatMessage.additional_kwargs`
+mapping. Missing provenance, audit outage, malformed output, and non-result
+verdicts fail before the wrapped memory receives the message.
+
+Runnable adapter and isolated tests:
+
+https://github.com/AInoAKARI/keymaster-mcp/tree/main/integrations/llamaindex-result-claim-audit
+
+Apply this patch:
+
+```bash
+curl -L https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AInoAKARI/keymaster-mcp/main/patches/run-llama-llama-index-result-claim-audit.patch | git apply
+```
+
+Verification:
+
+```bash
+python -m unittest -v test_llamaindex_result_claim_audit.py
+```
+
+The three isolated tests cover accepted receipt attachment, fail-closed
+rejection, and unchanged foreground writes without installing LlamaIndex or
+calling the network.
